WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.330
From its surprising cast to the slightly risqué
PG rating and its innovative shooting style,

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.380
there are more than a few things you should
know before you pick up your ticket to Detective

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:10.100
Pikachu.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.800
Here's all the background you need on the
world-famous Pokémon, the movie's unique

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.820
setting, and more.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.759
If you're not familiar with the world of Pokémon,
you might want to brush up before you head

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.100
into Detective Pikachu.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.620
Known as "Pocket Monsters" in its home country
of Japan, this series of video games came

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.900
to the United States in 1998 with Pokémon
Red and Blue for the Nintendo Game Boy, and

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.100
sold more copies than any other Game Boy game
besides Tetris.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.570
These blockbuster beginnings laid the groundwork
for a massive multimedia franchise, which

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.690
continued on to the Game Boy Advance all the
way up to the Nintendo Switch, with plenty

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.040
of spinoffs and tie-ins coming in along the
way.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:49.540
Between video games, movies, TV shows, a popular
trading card series and more, Pokémon has

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:54.010
secured its spot as the highest-grossing media
franchise of all time, but it all starts with

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:54.620
the games.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.760
In the main game series, players take on the
roles of Pokémon trainers, capturing wild

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.740
animal-monster hybrids that roam the world.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:05.640
These weaponized pets then get used in battles
with other trainers players encounter along

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.580
their journeys, as well as competitive Gym
Leaders, elite trainers, and even evil gangs

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.400
and corporations, from Pokémon Red and Blue's
Team Rocket to Pokémon Sun and Moon's Team

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:14.900
Skull.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.580
But for the most part, the games have always
come down to one goal: getting out in the

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.380
tall grass, hunting for Pokemon, and catching
'em all.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.280
Before Detective Pikachu referred to the live-action
movie, it was simply one of the franchise's

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.760
many spinoff video games.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.940
Released in 2018 for Nintendo's 3DS, Detective
Pikachu broke away from the loose narratives

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.920
and gameplay of the original games, setting
aside Gym badges and Pokémon catching to

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.790
focus instead on the story of a special talking
Pikachu, a type of "electric mouse" that is

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:46.020
arguably the franchise's most famous type
of Pokémon.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.200
In the game, the pocket monster teams up with
a young boy, Tim Goodman, who is the only

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.700
person who can understand Pikachu when he
speaks.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.840
Together, the two team up to search for Tim's
missing father and get to the bottom of a

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.200
sinister conspiracy.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.060
As Tim, Detective Pikachu lets the player
solve mysteries with their own talking Pikachu,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.380
evoking adventures from the Pokémon anime
series.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.920
The game received mixed reviews, but some
critics noted that it might make a better

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.240
movie than video game.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:15.200
Speaking of video games, the movie also evokes
the feel of Pokémon Yellow, one of the series'

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.000
first games.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.100
That unique take on Pokemon Red and Blue's
base game greatly increased the emphasis on

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.390
the player's relationship with their starter
Pokemon, in this case, a Pikachu who followed

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.440
behind you as you moved throughout the game.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.820
Though there have been plenty of animated
Pokémon movies over the decades, Detective

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:36.140
Pikachu marks the franchise's first live-action
film, adapting the story of a relatively new

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:36.640
game.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.400
Some longtime Pokémon fans were likely curious
about why this first live-action movie would

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:46.590
choose to focus on such a recent story rather
than continue the adventures of Ash, Misty,

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.600
and Brock from the cartoon series or original
films.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.900
Director Rob Letterman has opened up about
this decision, saying he wanted this film

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:58.730
to be set apart from what came before and
tell a story that felt new, especially considering

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:03.140
how many animated films have already focused
on the adventures of Ash Ketchum and friends.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.820
Thanks to the live actors, a film noir feel,
and strikingly lifelike CGI Pokémon, Detective

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.170
Pikachu should be able to make its mark on
the franchise with a totally fresh look and

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.190
not a lot of baggage.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:18.870
It will also be geared toward audiences of
both adults and children, with a PG rating

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.120
setting it apart from the typically G-rated
animated films.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:26.700
That way, parents and grown-up Pokémon nostalgics
should be able to enjoy the movie just as

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.120
much as the kids in the crowd.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.480
"Another round, extra shot, black as night.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.000
Thank you sweetie."

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.840
"LUDICOLO!!!!!"

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.160
Plenty of familiar faces are featured in Detective
Pikachu, including actors like Bill Nighy,

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.890
Chris Geere, and Ken Watanabe.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.180
But one performer you might not know yet is
Justice Smith, who plays the leading role

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.190
of Tim Goodman.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.190
"Stop talking!

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.190
You're a hallucination!"

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:46.960
"You're a hallucination."

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.060
As an actor, Smith has a small but impressive
resume, getting his start in television before

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:56.050
landing a supporting role in 2015's Paper
Towns, an adaptation of a popular young adult

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.300
novel by John Green.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.380
"Each Pokemon to understand the power that's
inside...

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.320
Pokemon!"

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:07.680
After that breakout, Smith found more success
when Baz Luhrmann cast him as the lead in

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.940
the ambitious Netflix series The Get Down.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:14.880
His largest pre-Pikachu role came in 2018
with Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.880
There, the actor played Franklin Webb, a computer
tech and hacker who helps track the dinosaurs

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.000
that have spread across the park.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.240
Now, with all the buzz that Detective Pikachu
is generating, it looks pretty likely that

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.140
this young actor's career is set to evolve
to the next level.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:28.980
"Turtle."

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:29.480
"Squirtle."

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:30.200
"Turtleman.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.740
Squirtle!"

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.540
Don't be fooled by the name of Detective Pikachu.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.140
After all, that's technically just the subtitle.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:41.040
The film also features plenty of other Pokémon
to remember and recognize.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.120
This includes creatures from the series' later
generations, like Aipom, Morelull, and Emolga,

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:50.130
but the most recognizable will likely be some
of the original 151.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:54.690
The three starting Pokémon from the series'
first generation, Bulbasaur, Squirtle, and

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:58.580
Charmander are all there, as well other favorites
such as Mr. Mime and Jigglypuff.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.700
"Enough with the games, say it…

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.220
Just say it!"

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:06.120
Just like in the games, many Pokémon won't
be spotted out in the wild, but rather as

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.160
companions to other human characters.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.720
Lucy Stevens, a reporter who helps Tim solve
mysteries in the movie, is accompanied by

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.860
her own personal Pokémon, a loyal Psyduck.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:20.060
One of the buzziest aspects of Detective Pikachu
is the unexpected voice behind the cuddly

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:20.560
creature.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.560
It's a hard thing to get right, how do you
win over audiences with an English-speaking

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.120
version of a famous electric mouse mostly
known for squeaking his own name?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.540
"You can hear him, right?"

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:30.950
"Pika pika!"

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:31.950
"Yeah!

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.840
Pika pika pika!"

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:37.040
While plenty of actors might come to mind,
Deadpool star Ryan Reynolds ended up snagging

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.590
the role, beating out equally off-the-wall
actor choices like Hugh Jackman, Dwayne "The

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.280
Rock" Johnson, and Danny Devito.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.860
But as the trailers have demonstrated, Reynolds'
take on the capable, witty, and slightly-bewildered

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.050
Detective Pikachu kind of makes sense.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:54.060
Thanks to his dry sense of humor and irony,
which viewers have proven themselves to love

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:58.370
so much in Deadpool, Reynolds is turning out
to be an inspired choice to play this irreverent,

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.660
yet brilliant Pikachu.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.920
"Oh my God, you can understand me!"

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.420
"Stop."

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.420
"I've been so lonely!"

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.960
Though Reynolds had a rough few years as an
actor, appearing in several box office flops,

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:11.220
his career was completely revived by 2016's
Deadpool.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:15.560
Since playing the foul-mouthed, deeply sarcastic
superhero, he's fully returned to Hollywood's

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.060
A-list.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.800
Now he's offering a new take on Pikachu that
could potentially help to make the mighty

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.360
mouse more popular than ever.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:26.620
In November 2018, some lucky viewers got the
chance to see a test screening of Detective

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.800
Pikachu, and early reactions have apparently
been quite positive.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:34.060
Audiences have specifically praised Reynolds'
voice acting and his chemistry with star Justice

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:34.800
Smith.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:39.640
The movie's CGI effects also earned some praise,
with viewers describing them as being extremely

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.360
lifelike even though they weren't quite finished
yet.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:47.000
Test screenings that followed this first rollout
have also reportedly garnered positive responses.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:51.280
What all of this means for Detective Pikachu,
besides potentially good reviews and box office

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:55.580
success, is that it could also hold the rare
distinction of being a well-received live-action

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:59.360
video game movie, a feat which has often seemed
impossible for Hollywood to pull off.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:03.770
From infamously bad films like Super Mario
Brothers and Street Fighter to more recent,

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:07.860
ill-advised efforts such as Assassin's Creed
and Warcraft, video game movies are pretty

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.340
much known for being terrible.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:13.500
But it's looking quite possible that Detective
Pikachu could break the mold by becoming one

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.760
of the first live-action movies based off
a video game to earn widespread audience and

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.760
critical acclaim.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:23.860
Thanks to its innovative CGI work, audiences
might expect that Detective Pikachu was shot

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:27.060
with a heavy emphasis on motion-capture suits
and green screen.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:31.320
But as star Justice Smith told New York Magazine,
that definitely wasn't the case.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:35.780
According to Smith, the production made a
point of shooting on location as much as possible,

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.820
using actual environments to help enhance
the reality of this live-action Pokemon world.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:45.080
Filming took place in both London and Scotland,
keeping green screens to a minimum and using

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:48.300
the locations' natural beauty and urban backdrops
to great effect.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.980
Director Rob Letterman reportedly wanted to
juxtapose the fantastical world of Pokémon

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:57.440
against a gritty urban landscape to make the
creatures, according to Smith, "pop more."

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.940
Also helping add to the distinctive look of
the movie is the fact that it was shot on

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:05.680
film, with the naturally grainy quality helping
to make the movie feel like a realistic and

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.680
gritty film noir.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:10.560
It's the sort of small detail you might not
have noticed on its own: instead, viewers

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.930
are just left with the impression that the
movie looks way more realistic than they may

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:14.740
have expected.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.990
In this way and others, Detective Pikachu
will visibly set itself apart from any of

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:23.570
its animated predecessors in the Pokemon series,
perhaps laying the track for a whole new tradition

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:25.380
for the franchise on the big screen.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:30.259
When the first trailer for Detective Pikachu
dropped in November 2018, audiences were both

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.740
confused and delighted.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:35.740
Compared to every other Pokemon property,
it looked very different, but it also had

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:36.720
a lot of charm.

00:08:36.789 --> 00:08:40.920
The first appearance of the title character,
combining the cutesy look of Pikachu with

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:44.850
the quippy Ryan Reynolds, went over with viewers
surprisingly well.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:49.310
Before long, a curious consensus started growing:
maybe the filmmakers had something here.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:53.270
The first trailer introduced the basic story
of Pikachu and Tim's quest to find his missing

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:56.800
father, but it also made sure viewers got
glimpses of other Pokémon.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:01.140
It also made it clear that this Pikachu would
be a slightly more grown-up iteration of the

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:05.430
beloved children's character, getting adult
fans who grew up with the series more interested

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.880
in the movie than they might have expected
they would be.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:13.420
The second trailer, released in February 2019,
featured even more Pokémon alongside Pikachu,

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:17.680
including the first glimpse of Mewtwo, the
menacing and hyper-intelligent Pokemon who

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.020
headlined the series' first animated movie
in 1998.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:25.360
The excitement and acclaim that Detective
Pikachu's first trailers kicked up has clearly

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.550
been encouraging to the people behind the
movie.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:31.070
Ahead of the film's release, it's already
been announced that there's a sequel in the

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:35.240
works, with a script being written by Oren
Uziel, best known for his writing credits

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:39.960
on 22 Jump Street, The Cloverfield Paradox,
and the upcoming Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.270
Whether or not the director or stars would
return for a sequel, or what a sequel to the

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.500
movie would even be about, it's still up in
the air.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:50.760
But if Detective Pikachu does well enough
with audiences at the box office, especially

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:54.990
against the summer movie juggernaut of Avengers:
Endgame, we wouldn't be surprised if it kicked

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.740
off a whole new cinematic universe of live-action
Pokemon adventures.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:03.140
For a movie this off-the-wall and unexpected,
that'd be a pretty shocking result.

